Overview

A class of language models that use deep-learning algorithms and are trained on extremely large textual datasets that can be multiple terabytes in size. LLMs can be classed into two types: generative or discriminatory. Generative LLMs are models that output text, such as the answer to a question or even writing an essay on a specific topic. They are typically unsupervised or semi-supervised learning models that predict what the response is for a given task…";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:2:{s:46:"sidebar:categories:ai_emerging_technologies:ai";b:1;s:43:"sidebar:categories:ai_emerging_technologies";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1741824278;s:8:"modified";i:1744171835;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Aditya Seth";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1744171835;s:2:"ip";s:14:"73.235.164.232";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:47:"sidebar:categories:ai_emerging_technologies:llm";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:-231;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Aditya Seth";}}}